# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
# Every request needs a session: send "Login" in auth.http first.
# Tip: `npm run seed:sample` creates a user with ~6 months of data (see prisma/seedSample.ts).
# Amounts are in cents and only CONFIRMED records count (PENDING ones are left out).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### Summary of a month: income, expense and balance
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/summary?month=2026-11

### Expenses by category (type defaults to EXPENSE), highest first
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/by-category?month=2026-11

### Income by category
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/by-category?month=2026-11&type=INCOME

### Income and expense of the last 6 months, ending at `month` (months defaults to 6)
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/monthly?month=2026-11

### Last 12 months (from 1 to 24)
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/monthly?month=2026-11&months=12


### ---------- Error cases ----------

### 400: `month` is required (the frontend decides the current month in the user's time zone)
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/summary

### 400: month 13 does not exist
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/summary?month=2026-13

### 400: more than 24 months
GET {{baseUrl}}/stats/monthly?month=2026-11&months=99
